node_modules/
dist/
# The desktop installers electron-builder writes (#565). Built on demand by
# `.github/workflows/desktop.yml`, never committed — they are ~100 MB each.
dist-desktop/
# The server's runtime dependency closure, resolved at packaging time by
# `packages/app/scripts/vendor-runtime.mjs` (#565).
dist-vendor/
coverage/
scratchpad/
# Swarm state is per-machine (lanes.json and friends) — EXCEPT coupling.txt and
# prd-milestones.txt, which are shared knowledge: coupling.txt is the list of
# files a fence cannot see coming, that `scripts/fence-lint.sh` refuses to run
# without; prd-milestones.txt is the committed PRD milestone manifest the
# location law reads so the suite can run offline. Written `.swarm/*` and not
# `.swarm/`, because git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is
# excluded — with `.swarm/` the negation below is silently inert and the
# tracked lint keeps failing "create one" on every clone but the author's.
.swarm/*
!.swarm/coupling.txt
!.swarm/prd-milestones.txt

# Agent instructions. NEITHER AGENTS.md NOR CLAUDE.md IS IGNORED, and neither
# may be — together they are the only mechanism by which four contributors'
# agents share conventions.
#
#   AGENTS.md        the runbook. Read natively by codex and friends.
#   CLAUDE.md        a one-line `@AGENTS.md` import. Claude Code reads
#                    CLAUDE.md and NOT AGENTS.md, so without this file a
#                    Claude session loads no project instructions at all.
#   CLAUDE.local.md  per-contributor, ignored below. This is where personal
#                    tooling notes go.
#
# Both were ignored here between 2d77e5b and #399, on the reasoning that
# "nothing in the tree cites either file" — a test run against tracked files
# only, while every issue brief cites AGENTS.md. The result was a repo with no
# runbook at all: #379's `.workmux.yaml` copy spent that whole period copying
# files that did not exist anywhere on disk. If you are about to re-add either
# one here, read #399 first.
#
# CLAUDE.local.md is the one of the three that is personal BY DEFINITION, so
# unlike the other two it must never become tracked at all.
CLAUDE.local.md

# Agent CLI working state. Both of these run inside this repo — codex under
# `codex exec -C`, claude in the worktrees the fleet creates — and each drops
# a local directory of settings and session state that is nobody else's
# business. Ignored here rather than in a personal global excludes file, so a
# contributor who has not set one up does not find them in `git status`.
.claude/
.codex/

# Audit findings — a dated snapshot of one reader's pass over the tree, not a
# ruling and not a record anything cites. Kept out of git deliberately: a
# findings list goes stale the moment the findings are fixed, and a stale one
# tracked in `docs/` reads like current state. What survives an audit belongs in
# an issue, a ruling, or a law test — not here.
docs/audit/

# Team-server deploy secrets, generated by packages/team/deploy/init.sh — never
# committed (prd-51 ruling 13, #433). The temp path is the atomic write's own
# intermediate (init.sh writes "$ENV_FILE.tmp.$$" before mv'ing it onto .env)
# and carries the same two secrets until the mv completes — an interrupted or
# failed run leaves it behind, so it needs the same ignore as the destination,
# not just the destination (found in review, #433).
packages/team/deploy/.env
packages/team/deploy/.env.tmp.*
